class.description:
Holds only the [member velocity] state needed to continue a damped-spring simulation from one call to [method update] to the next. [DampedSpring2D] doesn't store the spring's current value or target itself -- both are passed into [method update] each time, along with a [DampedSpringParameters] resource describing how the spring should respond.
This lets a single [DampedSpring2D] instance be reused for different values and targets, and lets one [DampedSpringParameters] resource be shared by many springs at once. A common use is smoothing a [Node2D]'s [member Node2D.position] toward some target position, as in a camera or drag-and-follow effect.
See also [DampedSpring] and [DampedSpring3D] for the [float]/[Vector3] equivalents.
[codeblock]
var spring := DampedSpring2D.new()
@export var spring_params: DampedSpringParameters

func _process(delta: float) -> void:
    follower.position = spring.update(delta, follower.position, target.position, spring_params)
[/codeblock]
